    "tabs": [
      {
        "id": "calc",
        "label": "Calc",
        "icon": "calculate"
      },
      {
        "id": "convert",
        "label": "Convert",
        "icon": "swap"
      },
      {
        "id": "graph",
        "label": "Graph",
        "icon": "chart"
      },
      {
        "id": "tools",
        "label": "Tools",
        "icon": "tools"
      },
      {
        "id": "clock",
        "label": "Clock",
        "icon": "clock"
      },
      {
        "id": "history",
        "label": "History",
        "icon": "history"
      }
    ],
    "_doc_modes": "One entry per mode. `kind` picks the renderer: expression (input + autocomplete + keypad + result), catalog (engine items listed by category, tap to evaluate), converter (value + from/to units of an engine category), form (declared fields substituted into declared expressions), plot (y = f(x) sampled by the engine), meter (microphone level + spectrum; the permission is asked only when this mode opens), history (past results and the engine's own variables). `options` is the engine's eval options JSON (libs/calc EvalOptions: in_base, out_base, precision, angle, approx 0 exact/1 exact where possible/2 decimal, mixed_units, unicode). A key is a string inserted as typed, or {label, insert}; the labels AC, DEL and = are the three actions. #768 the Clock tab adds six kinds whose data is the mode's `clock` object: worldclock (`zones`, the cities shown until the user edits the list; any id of the device's tzdata), alarms (`snooze_choices`/`snooze_default` minutes, `ring_minutes` before a ring silences itself, `vibrate_default`), timers (`presets` in seconds), stopwatch, interval (`presets`: work/rest/long_rest seconds, `long_every` rounds, `rounds`), bedtime (`sleep_choices` minutes for the sleep timer, which stops other apps' playback by taking audio focus; `bedtime_default` for the nightly reminder, a quiet alarm). Clock state lives in SharedPreferences `cloud_clock`, every wakeup is an AlarmManager alarm re-planned from it on boot, update and time/zone change, and a foreground service keeps anything running visible and controllable with the app closed.",
