    "_doc_debug_api": "The routes this app adds to the fleet debug API (libs:devtools AppDebugServer), so a calculation can be checked with the screen locked: /api/calc/eval?expr=&mode= evaluates through the bound engine with that mode's options, /api/calc/modes lists ui.modes, /api/calc/info is the engine handshake + engine info. #768 the Clock section registers a second group, build.json::ui.debug_api.clock_group (/api/clock/*), so alarms and timers can be checked and driven with the screen locked: status (every alarm, timer, the stopwatch, interval, sleep timer and what is ringing, each with its planned wakeup and whether AlarmManager really holds a PendingIntent for it, plus canScheduleExactAlarms and the system's next alarm clock), timer_start?seconds=&label= / timer_cancel?id= (a real timer through the same engine the screen uses), alarm_add?time=HH:MM&days=&label= / alarm_delete?id=, dismiss?key=. The op is `status`, not `state`: 1_cicd/src/data/update-ack-guard.json owns the `state` branch key of every `when (op)` route table for GET /api/state.",
    "debug_api": {
      "group": "calc",
      "clock_group": "clock"
    }
